# The .pkl data files are no longer tracked here: the large ones ride on the
# proteusPy data release as assets (see proteusPy/data_fetch.py) and the small
# ones are ordinary git blobs. Release-asset downloads are unmetered, where a
# single clone of the LFS-tracked database exhausted the whole monthly LFS
# bandwidth quota.
#
# Nothing is tracked through Git LFS any more. The notebooks, and one CSV,
# were the last files that were; their LFS objects were purged with the rest,
# so every fresh clone failed at checkout until they were recommitted as
# ordinary blobs (2026-09-18). Notebooks are committed with their outputs
# cleared, which is what keeps them small.
